# Graphics and diagrams

Read `.cursor/skills/databricks-visual-language/graphics.md` before adding or replacing UI visuals.

Quinovo’s mark is the primitive: **square nodes**, diamond/orthogonal strokes, **one Lava square**, navy structure, oat stage. Inline SVG only.

Must-haves on the landing page:

1. Hero **right column** = large cycle, layer stack, or framed workspace mockup (not a CSS glow).
2. How-it-works = **wide architecture SVG** with pipeline flow, not a text loop rail.
3. Feature cards = **120px+ SVG headers**, not Lucide-in-a-box.

```svg
<!-- ✅ square station, square cap, lava focal -->
<rect x="8" y="8" width="24" height="24" fill="#ff3621"/>
<path d="M32 20 H80" stroke="#1b3139" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="square"/>

<!-- ❌ explanation pretending to be a diagram -->
<span class="loop-node">Data</span><span>→</span><span class="loop-node">Propose</span>
```

No undraw/humaaans, no purple AI glow, no hotlinked images. Extra hues (`--blue`, `--green`, …) only **inside** diagrams, never on nav or buttons.
